.SH NAME
messq-backup - snapshot a data directory with VACUUM INTO


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq backup  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a consistent, self-verifying snapshot of a messq data directory into a single file via SQLite's VACUUM INTO on a read-only connection.

.PP
The snapshot works while the daemon runs AND after it stops, is written to a private temp directory, and renamed into place only after its own self-check passes. Provenance is stamped into the file itself so it explains its origin to whoever restores it later.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	source data directory holding messq.db

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	overwrite an existing destination (still temp+rename, never partial)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for backup

.PP
\fB--verify\fP="quick"
	post-snapshot self-check: quick|full|none


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq backup /var/backups/messq/$(date -u +%FT%H%MZ).db --data-dir /var/lib/messq
  messq backup /tmp/snap.db --data-dir /var/lib/messq --verify full --force
.EE


